Test oracles
------------

Not in the repository: `make` fetches each at the pinned commit into
`external/`, which Git ignores, or Cargo fetches it at the version
`Cargo.lock` pins, for tests only.  Nothing of them is
built into, linked with or distributed with the project's crates; the
`cpu32-oracle` and `cpu32-harness` crates that use them are
`publish = false`.

  Musashi          github.com/kstenerud/Musashi, commit
                   313ebf1bd9f4d0d93341eb5ce21fd8a119e9dbdd
                   (2026-03-08), Musashi 3.32.  MIT License,
                   Copyright Karl Stenerud (readme.txt, m68kconf.h).
                   A black-box differential oracle in 68020 mode
                   (`make oracle`, the `musashi` feature): built by
                   crates/cpu32-oracle/build.rs and driven through its
                   public API (m68k.h) only.  Its implementation is
                   not read to write the core, and none of its code is
                   in the core.  Its bundled SoftFloat (softfloat/,
                   SoftFloat Release 2b, John R. Hauser's license, not
                   MIT) is compiled with it because Musashi's headers
                   require it; the FPU is never used.
  Unicorn          github.com/unicorn-engine/unicorn, through the
                   unicorn-engine crate 2.1.5 (crates.io; it bundles
                   Unicorn 2.1.4 and QEMU's m68k), m68k only.  GPL-2.0.
                   A black-box oracle for the firmware corpus in 68020
                   mode (`make corpus-unicorn`, the `unicorn` feature of
                   cpu32-oracle and cpu32-harness, off by default and
                   not in `make ci`): fetched by Cargo, built from C,
                   driven through the crate's API only, in test binaries
                   that are never distributed and never linked into the
                   shipped crates.  The core is written from the
                   Motorola manuals, not from Unicorn or QEMU, and
                   none of their code or structure is here; Unicorn's
                   faults are known by behavior (crates/cpu32-oracle/src/
                   unicorn.rs, crates/cpu32/tests/unicorn_faults.rs).
  SingleStepTests  github.com/SingleStepTests/m68000, commit
  m68000           64b253116a3de04aaac4346c43680960dc9b67e5.  MIT
                   License, Copyright (c) 2024 SingleStepTests.  Test
                   cases generated from MAME's 68000 core
                   (`make singlestep`); read as data only.
